{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A double flat accidental."}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlaccidentalvalue\/flatflat"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"flatFlat"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}],"kind":"declarations"}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLAccidentalValue\/flatFlat"},"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Case","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL18MXLAccidentalValueO8flatFlatyA2CmF","title":"MXLAccidentalValue.flatFlat","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"flatFlat"}],"symbolKind":"case","role":"symbol"},"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLAccidentalValue"]]},"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","title":"IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLAccidentalValue":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The accidental-value type represents notated accidentals supported by MusicXML. In the MusicXML 2.0 DTD this"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"was a string with values that could be included. The XSD strengthens the data typing to an enumerated list."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The quarter- and three-quarters- accidentals are Tartini-style quarter-tone accidentals. The -down and -up"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"accidentals are quarter-tone accidentals that include arrows pointing down or up. The slash- accidentals are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"used in Turkish classical music. The numbered sharp and flat accidentals are superscripted versions of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"accidental signs, used in Turkish folk music. The sori and koron accidentals are microtonal sharp and flat"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"accidentals used in Iranian and Persian music. The other accidental covers accidentals other than those listed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"here. It is usually used in combination with the smufl attribute to specify a particular SMuFL accidental. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"smufl attribute may be used with any accidental value to help specify the appearance of symbols that share the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"same MusicXML semantics."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlaccidentalvalue","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLAccidentalValue"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"MXLAccidentalValue","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLAccidentalValue"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLAccidentalValue","role":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLAccidentalValue/flatFlat":{"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"flatFlat"}],"type":"topic","title":"MXLAccidentalValue.flatFlat","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLAccidentalValue\/flatFlat","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlaccidentalvalue\/flatflat","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A double flat accidental."}],"kind":"symbol"}}}